1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,478
This is the last lecture of the class,

2
00:00:03,928 --> 00:00:06,972
and it puts the whole class together.

3
00:00:07,872 --> 00:00:12,654
You have a boss, with ships and objectives and a hook.

4
00:00:13,104 --> 00:00:18,757
And you know how to write a scene, a call, and an answer.

5
00:00:20,557 --> 00:00:22,730
Today, at last, she speaks.

6
00:00:23,630 --> 00:00:29,283
And all of her voice goes in the one file you already have.

7
00:00:30,483 --> 00:00:35,265
Last time, the crew had ten minutes to sink the Morrigan,

8
00:00:35,715 --> 00:00:39,628
and nothing warned them as the time ran down.

9
00:00:40,528 --> 00:00:42,267
Two lines fix that.

10
00:00:43,167 --> 00:00:45,776
Speaker says who gives the warning,

11
00:00:46,226 --> 00:00:51,878
and here it's a role: the name of her flagship, in small letters.

12
00:00:52,778 --> 00:00:55,387
Signal says is what she sends.

13
00:00:57,187 --> 00:01:01,100
Where I write the word time, in curly brackets,

14
00:01:01,550 --> 00:01:05,028
the game puts in the time that's left.

15
00:01:05,928 --> 00:01:11,580
It's sent at five minutes, at two, at one, and at thirty seconds,

16
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:15,943
and only the ones that fit inside your limit.

17
00:01:17,143 --> 00:01:19,752
Now run lint, and it complains.

18
00:01:20,652 --> 00:01:23,696
It says morrigan isn't in the cast.

19
00:01:25,496 --> 00:01:28,104
And here, that warning is wrong.

20
00:01:29,004 --> 00:01:32,917
Lint's looking for a person, in a Characters section,

21
00:01:33,367 --> 00:01:35,976
and the Morrigan is a ship.

22
00:01:36,876 --> 00:01:39,920
The game looks for a character first,

23
00:01:40,370 --> 00:01:45,587
and then for a ship wearing that role, and it finds her.

24
00:01:46,487 --> 00:01:53,443
So this is the only warning in the whole course that I'll tell you to keep.

25
00:01:54,343 --> 00:01:56,517
Read it every time, though.

26
00:01:56,967 --> 00:02:02,620
If the name in it isn't on your Named line, then it's true.

27
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:07,733
For testing, I've set the limit to three minutes.

28
00:02:08,633 --> 00:02:11,241
She arrives, and I do nothing.

29
00:02:12,141 --> 00:02:16,924
About a minute later, Comms gets a message from the Morrigan,

30
00:02:17,374 --> 00:02:20,417
with the objective's name as its title.

31
00:02:22,217 --> 00:02:24,826
You have one fifty-nine, little ship.

32
00:02:25,276 --> 00:02:27,450
Then this sector is mine.

33
00:02:28,350 --> 00:02:30,959
That's her voice, in my words,

34
00:02:31,409 --> 00:02:34,017
and it's in the one file.

35
00:02:34,917 --> 00:02:40,135
If I send that file to a friend, they hear it too.

36
00:02:41,335 --> 00:02:43,509
Now for the call itself.

37
00:02:44,409 --> 00:02:48,322
You know the three parts from your own mission:

38
00:02:48,772 --> 00:02:53,120
a Beat that places it, a cast, and a scene.

39
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:57,063
All three go in the boss file,

40
00:02:57,513 --> 00:03:00,122
and I start with the Beat.

41
00:03:01,922 --> 00:03:07,574
It has an Action line that says, queen hails, and a scene's key.

42
00:03:08,474 --> 00:03:11,952
I run lint, and there's a second warning.

43
00:03:12,852 --> 00:03:14,591
This one is true.

44
00:03:15,491 --> 00:03:19,839
The Beat names a scene that nobody has written yet,

45
00:03:20,289 --> 00:03:23,333
so right now, no call would come.

46
00:03:24,533 --> 00:03:28,880
So I go to the very end of the file,

47
00:03:29,330 --> 00:03:32,809
and I type two sections you already know.

48
00:03:33,709 --> 00:03:37,187
Characters, with the Queen and her first mate.

49
00:03:38,087 --> 00:03:40,261
And Dialogue, with one scene.

50
00:03:42,061 --> 00:03:45,539
The sections have two hashes, like her objectives,

51
00:03:45,989 --> 00:03:50,337
and the people and the scenes inside them have three.

52
00:03:51,237 --> 00:03:55,585
The scene is just what you wrote in Lecture 3:

53
00:03:56,035 --> 00:03:59,948
a speaker, two blocks of takes, and an answer.

54
00:04:00,848 --> 00:04:03,022
That answer finishes the Beat.

55
00:04:04,822 --> 00:04:06,561
I run lint again,

56
00:04:07,011 --> 00:04:10,489
and the warning about the call has gone.

57
00:04:11,689 --> 00:04:14,298
There's nothing to paste for this.

58
00:04:15,198 --> 00:04:19,111
When she arrives, the Siege reads her file itself.

59
00:04:20,011 --> 00:04:22,620
Her objectives go to the crew,

60
00:04:23,070 --> 00:04:25,678
her people come into the game,

61
00:04:26,128 --> 00:04:30,041
and her scenes are made ready to be called.

62
00:04:31,841 --> 00:04:34,015
Two things follow from that.

63
00:04:34,915 --> 00:04:37,959
Her people don't exist until she arrives,

64
00:04:38,409 --> 00:04:41,887
which is fine, because her Beats don't either.

65
00:04:42,787 --> 00:04:46,700
And her card isn't part of this at all.

66
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:50,209
It still brings the third ship,

67
00:04:50,659 --> 00:04:54,137
and I haven't added a line to it.

68
00:04:55,337 --> 00:04:57,946
Now I make an answer matter.

69
00:04:58,846 --> 00:05:02,324
A second answer leads to a second scene,

70
00:05:02,774 --> 00:05:06,687
where the Badb's first mate comes on the line.

71
00:05:07,587 --> 00:05:11,500
And if the crew says, then fly with us,

72
00:05:11,950 --> 00:05:14,559
three things happen after the semicolon.

73
00:05:16,359 --> 00:05:18,098
The call is finished.

74
00:05:18,998 --> 00:05:23,346
Turn the Badb is finished, which reveals one more step.

75
00:05:24,246 --> 00:05:28,159
And that step has an Action of its own:

76
00:05:28,609 --> 00:05:30,783
badb joins T S N.

77
00:05:31,683 --> 00:05:33,857
So the ship changes sides.

78
00:05:35,657 --> 00:05:38,700
Notice where I typed those two records:

79
00:05:39,150 --> 00:05:42,193
among her objectives, above the Characters line.

80
00:05:43,093 --> 00:05:47,441
Her people and her scenes stay last in the file.

81
00:05:48,641 --> 00:05:51,250
Check both, and then play it.

82
00:05:52,150 --> 00:05:56,498
There's her call, waiting, with her name and the title.

83
00:05:57,398 --> 00:06:00,441
I open it, she makes her offer,

84
00:06:00,891 --> 00:06:03,935
and I talk to the Badb instead.

85
00:06:05,735 --> 00:06:07,474
Then fly with us.

86
00:06:08,374 --> 00:06:13,157
The crew's told the call is done, the Badb is turned,

87
00:06:13,607 --> 00:06:17,085
and the bonus for sinking her is closed.

88
00:06:17,985 --> 00:06:19,724
That's a real choice:

89
00:06:20,174 --> 00:06:23,217
three hundred credits, or one raider fewer.

90
00:06:24,117 --> 00:06:27,161
Then play it again and refuse her,

91
00:06:27,611 --> 00:06:32,393
and play it a third time and never answer at all.

92
00:06:33,293 --> 00:06:37,207
The game has to be winnable on every road.

93
00:06:38,407 --> 00:06:41,015
Now, what are you handing over?

94
00:06:41,915 --> 00:06:45,393
Nearly all of her is the one file.

95
00:06:46,293 --> 00:06:48,467
Send just that one file,

96
00:06:48,917 --> 00:06:53,265
and your friend gets the boss, her ships, her objectives,

97
00:06:53,715 --> 00:06:55,889
the Morrigan calling the clock,

98
00:06:56,339 --> 00:07:01,122
and the Queen's call with the answer that turns the Badb.

99
00:07:02,922 --> 00:07:08,139
What they don't get is the arrival line and the reserve ship.

100
00:07:09,039 --> 00:07:10,778
Those are her card,

101
00:07:11,228 --> 00:07:15,576
and the card lives in a folder inside Legendary Missions.

102
00:07:16,476 --> 00:07:20,824
An update removes that folder, for them and for you.

103
00:07:21,724 --> 00:07:24,767
So keep a copy outside the game.

104
00:07:25,667 --> 00:07:30,015
Lint will tell you: one warning when the folder's there,

105
00:07:30,465 --> 00:07:32,639
and two when it isn't.

106
00:07:33,839 --> 00:07:36,448
The page ends with a rubric,

107
00:07:36,898 --> 00:07:41,680
and every line on it is something you can check yourself.

108
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:46,493
She's yours, she's checked, she plays, and she travels.

109
00:07:48,293 --> 00:07:52,207
When every line is ticked, you've finished Class 2.

110
00:07:53,107 --> 00:07:56,150
You can write a cast, a conversation,

111
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:59,209
and a boss who talks back.

112
00:08:00,109 --> 00:08:04,022
In the next class, the crew leaves the bridge.
